var ITEMS=[["What bike mechanics do","Bicycle mechanics assemble, tune, and repair bikes: shifting, braking, wheels, bearings, and suspension. From flat fixes to full builds, it is precise mechanical work with happy customers. Barnett or UBI school plus shop"], ["Essential tools","Hex wrench set, Torx set, cable cutters, chain tool, chain whip and cassette lockring tool, cone wrenches, spoke wrench, pedal wrench, torque wrench, tire levers, floor pump, and a repair stand. Pros add: truing stand an"], ["Key skills","Derailleur adjustment: limit screws, then cable tension. Brake setup: pad alignment and cable tension. Wheel truing: lateral, radial, dish. Bearing service: hubs, bottom brackets, headsets. Tubeless setup. Reading wear: "], ["Safety essentials","Torque carbon parts to spec \u2014 over-tightening cracks frames. Test brakes before every test ride. Stand stability: secure the bike. Chemical safety with degreasers. Test ride carefully after major work."], ["Getting started","Work on your own bikes first, then volunteer at co-ops. Barnett Bicycle Institute or UBI for formal training. Start at a shop doing flats and tunes; build to wheels and suspension. E-bike certification is the growth area"], ["Pro tips","Clean the bike before diagnosing \u2014 grime hides problems. Replace cables and housing together. Measure chain wear; it saves cassettes. Document e-bike systems carefully. A test ride is part of every repair."], ["Derailleur","Trade term \u2014 Derailleur: The mechanism moving the chain between gears."], ["Limit screws","Trade term \u2014 Limit screws: Set derailleur travel extremes."], ["Barrel adjuster","Trade term \u2014 Barrel adjuster: Fine-tunes cable tension."], ["Chain wear","Trade term \u2014 Chain wear: Elongation; replace at 0.5-0.75%."], ["Cassette","Trade term \u2014 Cassette: The rear gear cluster."], ["Chainring","Trade term \u2014 Chainring: The front gears."], ["Bottom bracket","Trade term \u2014 Bottom bracket: The crank axle bearings."], ["Headset","Trade term \u2014 Headset: The fork steering bearings."], ["Truing","Trade term \u2014 Truing: Straightening wheels."], ["Dish","Trade term \u2014 Dish: Wheel centering between hub flanges."], ["Spoke tension","Trade term \u2014 Spoke tension: Even tension makes strong wheels."], ["Tubeless","Trade term \u2014 Tubeless: Sealant-based tire system without tubes."], ["Disc brake","Trade term \u2014 Disc brake: Rotor and caliper braking."], ["Rim brake","Trade term \u2014 Rim brake: Pad-on-rim braking."], ["Torque spec","Trade term \u2014 Torque spec: Critical for carbon parts."], ["Dropout","Trade term \u2014 Dropout: The frame slots holding wheel axles."], ["Thru-axle","Trade term \u2014 Thru-axle: Stiff bolt-through wheel attachment."], ["Quick release","Trade term \u2014 Quick release: Cam-action wheel attachment."], ["Suspension sag","Trade term \u2014 Suspension sag: Proper shock setup baseline."]];
